  "version": "as-filed",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id) not stated.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.\n(other) Election Code, returns: sets a deadline to decide appeals from county board of elections decisions and for the Secretary to tabulate/compute/canvass returns; recounts and contests: effect of decision and appeal. Committee-roll-call brief description: \"Establishes firm deadline to decide appeals of county Board of Elections, without limiting any right to appeal to align Pennsylvania with the new requirements of the federal Electoral Count Reform Act.\"\n(note) Off this topic: the bill sets no ID or citizenship-proof rule.",
